            <ArticleTitle>Local bupivacaine infusion following bone graft harvest from the iliac crest.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>400-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A method of local analgesic delivery to the donor site after the harvest of autogenous corticocancellous bone from the iliac crest is described. The technique reduces the need for postoperative systemic analgesia and facilitates early patient mobilization.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
